 ## Overview
-Grid Deformation is a preprocessing technique applied prior to data reduction in volume rendering compression. It transforms the input data grid according to user-defined regions to better preserve salient features during subsequent downsampling [S1][S2]. It is an orthogonal approach to hierarchical models like wavelets, reporting improved visual results compared to pure downsampling and wavelet-based methods [S1][S2].
